{
    "word": "medicaster",
    "lang_code": "en",
    "source_file_to_entries": {
        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "87a5eabc-a00f-3ce9-9ab7-fd025d7d4af9",
                "word": "medicaster",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "a212c24d-ea64-433e-ba0d-7f2d3890fd95",
                        "entry_id": "87a5eabc-a00f-3ce9-9ab7-fd025d7d4af9",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "medicasters"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "16ff0cb0-a74b-334d-b74c-c02f9db65ac6",
                        "entry_id": "87a5eabc-a00f-3ce9-9ab7-fd025d7d4af9",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A quack doctor; someone who pretends to have medical knowledge."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated",
                            "literary"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3216c1c-c33e-4a79-b870-5853ff82aa66",
                                "sense_id": "16ff0cb0-a74b-334d-b74c-c02f9db65ac6",
                                "text": "But these innovating Medicaſters have introduced a Practice not only very precarious, but in many Reſpects extremely dangerous, and quite devoid of any one of the Qualities which conſtitute a good Remedy, viz. to cure the Patient, as the Axiom has it, cito, tuto, & jucunde, i.e. ſpeedily, ſafely, and pleaſantly."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "7fdb786c-9faf-4fa4-90bf-5cfe64f67006",
                                "sense_id": "16ff0cb0-a74b-334d-b74c-c02f9db65ac6",
                                "text": "The most idiotic medicaster, when he had named, or, as they term it, diagnosticated a typhoid fever, found himself upon a level with the medical celebrities of the epoch. […] If the patient died, that was perfectly simple: he had a typhoid fever to which he was inevitably doomed to succumb! If he recovered, what a noble triumph for the medicaster, even when he had perhaps arbitrarily imposed the name of typhoid upon a simple and benignant fever, as is constantly done!"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "025d708d-e05e-4032-9f5e-da9b6b9b4706",
                                "sense_id": "16ff0cb0-a74b-334d-b74c-c02f9db65ac6",
                                "text": "[I]t [opium] is a double-edged sword, a divine gift in the hands of a master, a poison in those of a mere routinist—a medicaster—a demi-physician."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "f1173caf-7862-4556-a86d-d52ca66432d4",
                                "sense_id": "16ff0cb0-a74b-334d-b74c-c02f9db65ac6",
                                "text": "[I]f pushed, I would judge that many of those ‘medicasters’ and ‘charlatans’ commonly arraigned as tricksters were less cheats than zealots: if we are to speak of delusion, it is primarily self-delusion[…]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "95f0c5b3-9192-493e-8d0f-25a9b2b62729",
                        "source_entry_id": "87a5eabc-a00f-3ce9-9ab7-fd025d7d4af9",
                        "source_sense_id": "16ff0cb0-a74b-334d-b74c-c02f9db65ac6",
                        "source_sense_description": "quack doctor",
                        "target_lang_word": "médicastre",
                        "target_lang_code": "fr",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "médicastre",
                                "target_lang_code": "fr",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "532332c9-3b38-3710-9fb3-afd2e5ef02f2",
                                        "entry_id": "66d50def-4b5b-3e32-8fc7-60dd3d7316b5",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Médecin ignorant et hâbleur."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bcb756a6-36ae-4ad0-9164-2724b9468bc9",
                                                "sense_id": "532332c9-3b38-3710-9fb3-afd2e5ef02f2",
                                                "text": "À cette époque (1856), une médicastre sans aucun diplôme avait su capter la confiance des malades qui se rendaient en foule à ses consultations."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c5a0cf0b-b5e2-4c9c-93a4-bec38d7147c7",
                                                "sense_id": "532332c9-3b38-3710-9fb3-afd2e5ef02f2",
                                                "text": "De même qu’une lèpre, l’avidité du siècle ravageait l’Église, courbait des moines sur des inventaires et des factures, transformait les supérieurs en des confiseurs et des médicastres, les frères lais et les convers, en de vulgaires emballeurs et de bas potards."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "83d6bfe0-857c-48be-85de-97e3dc5cbd84",
                                                "sense_id": "532332c9-3b38-3710-9fb3-afd2e5ef02f2",
                                                "text": "On était enclin déjà, je pense, à juger la qualité et la compétence d'un médecin par le prix qu'il fait payer : plus il prend cher, et plus il doit être savant. Ce critérium s'applique encore davantage aux médicastres, aux voyantes et aux charlatans."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a84164a-2f0e-41dc-a602-b4cb3827eed4",
                                                "sense_id": "532332c9-3b38-3710-9fb3-afd2e5ef02f2",
                                                "text": "Anthime propose d’envoyer quérir un oculiste ; mais Marguerite connaît de réputation les médicastres italiens, et ne veut \"pour rien au monde\" en entendre parler."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c7fb362e-c9cb-478b-853c-956af8023b52",
                                                "sense_id": "532332c9-3b38-3710-9fb3-afd2e5ef02f2",
                                                "text": "Un infâme petit médicastre qui habitait naguère Hanovre et qui a déménagé un peu plus au sud pour fonder un sanatorium de quatre sous dans le Harz."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f0385de9-4f4f-49f1-bf5d-0dea87ee86a9",
                        "source_entry_id": "87a5eabc-a00f-3ce9-9ab7-fd025d7d4af9",
